    <string name="settings_two_pass" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Two-pass encoding</string>
    <string name="settings_two_pass_summary" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Analysis pass first, then the real encode with the statistics of the whole video: the size lands close to the target (short simple clips may stay below it), bits go where they are needed. AV1 software, VP9, H.264 (H.264 only with a bitrate). Takes about 10 to 30 percent longer</string>
    <string name="settings_two_pass_bitrate" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Two-pass video bitrate</string>
    <string name="settings_prefilter" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Filter once (FFV1 intermediate file)</string>
    <string name="settings_prefilter_summary" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Deinterlacing, border crop, denoising and scaling run once into a lossless FFV1 file in app storage, and both passes read it instead of filtering the source twice. Practically the same result, saves one whole filter run (with NL-means about 15 to 20 percent of the time). Needs about 4 GB free per 24-minute DVD episode at 480p while it is converted; without enough room the passes filter as usual. Not used for test excerpts</string>
    <string name="settings_av1_sw_speed" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">AV1 software speed (libaom cpu-used)</string>
    <string name="settings_av1_10bit" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">AV1 software in 10 bit</string>
    <string name="settings_av1_10bit_summary" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Less banding in gradients and dark scenes, usually a little smaller; slower to encode. Every AV1 decoder plays it</string>
    <string name="settings_denoise" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Denoise before encoding</string>
    <string name="settings_auto_crop" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Crop black borders automatically</string>
    <string name="settings_auto_crop_summary" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Scans the key frames of the whole video first (a minute or two) and removes black bars; letterboxed videos save a lot</string>
    <string name="settings_test_excerpt" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Test excerpt</string>
    <string name="settings_audio_bitrate" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Audio bitrate</string>
    <string name="settings_audio_channels" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Audio channels</string>
    <string name="settings_audio_track" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Audio track</string>
    <string name="settings_subtitles" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Subtitles</string>

    <string name="settings_long_encodes_title" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Long conversions</string>
    <string name="settings_keep_alive" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Keep converting with the screen off</string>
    <string name="settings_keep_alive_summary" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Foreground service with notification and wake lock: the conversion goes on when the screen turns off or another app is opened, and after 10 minutes the screen may time out. Off: it stops when you leave the screen (original behaviour)</string>
    <string name="settings_save_copy" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Save a copy to Movies/FFShare Deint</string>
    <string name="settings_save_copy_summary" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Finished videos are also copied there. The shared file in the cache is deleted after a while. Android 7 to 9 needs the storage permission for this, without it the copy goes to Android/data/…/files/Movies, which is deleted together with the app</string>

